1450	// ===================== persistent continuous-ring prefill (hd128 bf16 TMA) =====================
1451	// FA3-style persistent kernel: each CTA grabs work-items off a static stride (work = blockIdx.x +
1452	// k*gridDim.x) and processes them in a loop. The win vs the per-tile prefill_kernel is that the K/V
1453	// ring is ONE CONTINUOUS stream across work-items -- PipelineState (the ring index g + its phase) is
1454	// declared once and NEVER reset per item, so the producer prefetches the next item's K/V into slots
1455	// the consumer just freed, with no per-item pipeline-fill bubble. (The earlier naive per-item-reinit
1456	// persistent attempt regressed precisely because it paid that fill + barrier-reinit cost every item.)
1457	//
1458	// Q is single-buffered with a barQf/barQe ping-pong (phase = witer&1): the producer waits barQe (the
1459	// consumer freed the prior Q), reloads Q -- via ONE async TMA box-set (rep==1, mapQ) so the reload is
1460	// cheap enough to hide behind the continuous ring; GQA/paged would fall back to the cp.async gather --
1461	// then signals barQf. To keep the ring primed across the boundary the producer issues the item's FIRST
1462	// K/V tile (empty-gated on the global g, NOT Q-gated) BEFORE the barQe wait, then floods the rest after
1463	// Q. Stage index / phase everywhere use the GLOBAL counter g so
1464	// producer and consumer stay in lock-step (both advance g by n_cnt per non-empty item, skip empties
1465	// identically). num_splits is implicitly 1 (prefill); no split-KV epilogue. TMA-only (routed so).
